        "original_id": "0f385fda-4874-5746-9ffb-4aae2b6275f2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mick Jagger, Brett Scallions, Joan Jett, Rod Stewart, David Cassidy, Jane Fonda, Florence Henderson, Carl Bell, Jeff Abercrombie\n- Organizations: The Rolling Stones, Fuel\n- Products: Puppet Strings, Natural Selection\n- Topics: shag haircut\n\nFacts:\n- Mick Jagger was born on 26 July 1943.\n- Mick Jagger is an English singer-songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and composer.\n- Mick Jagger gained fame as the lead singer and a founder member of the Rolling Stones, a band active from 1962 to the present.\n- Brett Scallions was born on December 21, 1971.\n- Brett Scallions is an American musician.\n- The shag haircut became popular in the 1970s after being worn by celebrities including Joan Jett, Mick Jagger, Rod Stewart, David Cassidy, Jane Fonda, and Florence Henderson.\n- Puppet Strings was released on March 4, 2014.\n- Puppet Strings was Fuel's first studio album since 2003's Natural Selection to feature original lead singer Brett Scallions.\n- Puppet Strings was the first Fuel album not to feature original songwriter and guitarist Carl Bell and bassist Jeff Abercrombie.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
